  "details": "I've been trying to migrate an avatar that uses out-of-Head transforms with a Parent Constraint to the ear, into a inside-of-Head transforms with two VRCHeadChop components (one to make the Head invisible, and another one to make objects located within the Ear visible) without constraints.\n\nHowever, despite the Head being invisible (as expected) and the inside-of-Head transforms being visible (as expected), the position of those visible inside-of-Head transform appears to be incorrect in first person.\n\nThis position issue is the subject of this post, not the visibility.\n\nPicture below (Left is normal avatar, Right is VRCHeadChop migration):\n\nMy normal (non-HeadChop) avatar has an arrow model and a beam particle system constrained to my right ear. The right ear has a PhysBone, which is animated with mouth tracking, so in first person, I usually see the beam coming from the middle-right when my mouth is firmly closed, and the beam coming from the top-right otherwise.\n\nThe migrated version has the beam coming from the neck, which is incorrect.\n\nIn the mirror, the beam comes from the expected position.\n\nThis setup doesn't look much different from what the blog advertised ( https://global.discourse-cdn.com/business5/uploads/vrchat/original/3X/d/7/d7c5cc2b8d3bae9a78ed880beefe9557200412d5.mp4 ), it's practically equivalent to making the ears visible, I'd like to understand whether this is a bug or some incorrectly configured component.",
